# `lens-body`: a lens's body is a reference from its parameter, a lens path or a lens
# applied to one (Semantics ch. 5, "The borrow rule": "A lens's result is alive while its
# argument is", and "Nothing else makes a reference"); and its parameter is a reference,
# written with `&` ("A named lens takes `&` on its name and its one parameter").
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
type Regs = record:
    acc: Int
    x: Int

type Vm = record:
    pc: Nat
    regs: Regs

&Acc: fn &Vm -> &Int
fn &Acc &vm = 0

&Spare: fn &Vm -> &Int
fn &Spare vm = vm.regs.x

&Sum: fn &Vm -> &Int
fn &Sum &vm = &vm.regs.acc + &vm.regs.x
